# Production: connect to the ObjectStack server.
# Defaults to same-origin (empty). The published @object-ui/console
# package is meant to be embedded in any ObjectStack server, so we
# MUST NOT bake in a specific origin here. Demo-only deployments
# (e.g. demo.objectstack.ai on Vercel) inject VITE_SERVER_URL at
# build time via their deploy environment.
VITE_SERVER_URL=
VITE_USE_MOCK_SERVER=false

# ── Sentry error tracking: CONFIGURED ON THE SERVER, never here ─────────────
#
# ⛔ DO NOT COMMIT A DSN IN THIS FILE — under ANY variable name. The ratchet at
# packages/app-shell/src/observability/committed-telemetry-endpoint.test.ts
# fails CI if you do, and the reason is not style:
#
# `@object-ui/console` publishes a PRE-BUILT SPA (`files: ["dist"]`,
# `prepublishOnly: pnpm build`). ONE artifact, built once from this file, is
# what every consumer embeds — the hosted SaaS console AND the on-premises /
# air-gapped EE images. Vite inlines every `VITE_*` here into that bundle as a
# frozen object literal, so a DSN committed here is a live third-party
# telemetry endpoint compiled into the artifact that lands inside customer
# networks, and nothing on the deployed host can edit it back out.
#
# That is exactly what happened: an air-gapped EE deployment was measured
# sending 14 Sentry envelopes per session to sentry.io carrying IP and
# User-Agent PII, with no way for the customer to turn it off
# (objectstack-ai/cloud#1508, objectstack-ai/objectui#5522).
#
# ── There is nothing to set here any more (objectstack#12681) ───────────────
#
# The DSN and every knob that travels with it now arrive from the ObjectStack
# RUNTIME, on `GET /api/v1/runtime/config`. That is deliberate: ObjectStack's
# users consume this console PREBUILT and never run a build of it, so a
# build-time key was unreachable for them — they could neither turn reporting
# on nor turn PII collection off. Operators configure it on their server:
#
#   OS_TELEMETRY_CLIENT_ERROR_REPORTING_DSN=https://PUBLIC_KEY@HOST/PROJECT_ID
#   OS_TELEMETRY_CLIENT_ERROR_REPORTING_SEND_DEFAULT_PII=true   # off by default
#   OS_TELEMETRY_CLIENT_ERROR_REPORTING_ENVIRONMENT=production
#   OS_TELEMETRY_CLIENT_ERROR_REPORTING_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1
#   OS_TELEMETRY_CLIENT_ERROR_REPORTING_REPLAY_SAMPLE_RATE=0
#
# No runtime-served DSN ⇒ `initSentry()` returns false and `@sentry/react` is
# never even imported (the vendor-sentry chunk is not fetched). Turning
# reporting off is unsetting the server DSN — there is deliberately no
# build-time force-off left, because nobody consuming a prebuilt console could
# reach one. See apps/console/docs/error-tracking.md.
#
# ── The ONE build-time telemetry knob that survives ─────────────────────────
#
# A release identifies WHICH BUNDLE produced a stack trace and must match the
# source maps that bundle's pipeline uploaded — a property of the build, which
# no server can know. Inject it from your deploy environment, never here:
#
# VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=   # injected by CI as VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA when available
